================================================================================
NASA INTERNATIONAL SPACE APPS CHALLENGE 2026 - OPEN SCIENCE & RESEARCH NOTICE
================================================================================

1. Competition & Open-Science Context:
   This repository and its codebase were developed for the NASA International
   Space Apps Challenge 2026. The system is designed to provide autonomous,
   offline-first astronaut health evaluation and clinical decision-support during
   deep-space exploratory missions (such as Moon-to-Mars and Artemis transit) where
   real-time ground communications with Earth Mission Control encounter multi-minute
   speed-of-light delays or blackouts.

2. NASA Open Science Data Attribution:
   Biomarker distributions, physiological baseline thresholds, laboratory assay
   matrices, and mission profiles are derived from publicly accessible open science
   datasets provided by the NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR):
   - OSD-575 / OSD-569: Space Omics and Medical Atlas (SOMA) SpaceX Inspiration4 cohort.
   - NASA Technical Standard NASA-STD-3001: Space Flight Human-System Standard
     (Volume 1: Crew Health; Volume 2: Human Factors, Habitability, and Environmental Health).
   - NASA Human Research Program (HRP) Risk Mitigation Protocols.

3. Research & Demonstration Prototype Disclaimer:
   H.E.L.I.O.S. (Helix-Ai Analyst) is an experimental aerospace engineering and
   biomedical informatics software demonstrator. It is NOT a certified clinical
   medical device under FDA 510(k), EMA CE-mark, or equivalent regulatory frameworks.
   It is intended strictly for research, simulation, educational, and spaceflight
   habitability demonstration purposes.
